   "response_text": "All confirmed from the repo. Here's what the code says:\n\n**\ud83d\udc36 Findings from `httpx/_client.py`:**\n\n1. **TooManyRedirects raise line**: Line **972** is the line containing `raise TooManyRedirects(` \u2014 that's the sync `Client._send_handling_redirects` path. (The async client raises the exact same statement at line 1719, but the sync client's raise is the canonical one at 972.)\n\n2. **Status codes that can switch method to GET** (from `_redirect_method`):\n   - `303 SEE_OTHER` \u2192 GET (unless HEAD)\n   - `302 FOUND` \u2192 GET (unless HEAD)\n   - `301 MOVED_PERMANENTLY` \u2192 GET (only if POST)\n   - So: **301, 302, 303**\n\n3. **Headers removed when method switches to GET** (from `_redirect_headers`):\n   - `Content-Length`\n   - `Transfer-Encoding`\n   - So: **Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding**\n\n4. **Header removed on *every* redirect regardless of origin/method**:\n   - `headers.pop(\"Cookie\", None)` \u2014 unconditional, the client cookie store handles cookies instead.\n   - So: **Cookie**\n\nNice and DRY \u2014 that `_redirect_headers` helper is shared by both sync and async clients, so no duplication there. \ud83d\udc4d\n\nANSWER: 972|301, 302, 303|Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding|Cookie",
